    "A map from each original node to its copy answers two questions at once: have I seen this node, and which copy should I link to?",
    "Walk through the triangle in the first example: when you reach node 1 again from node 3, you must link to the copy you already made, not create a second one.",
    "DFS or BFS over the original with an original-to-copy dictionary: create a copy the first time you see a node, and append the copies of its neighbors to the copy's list."
  ],
